      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "We assign a 70% probability to a continued bullish trajectory for the AI infrastructure sector, driven by validated demand and sustained investment. A 20% probability is given to a neutral scenario where broader economic slowdowns temper, but do not halt, AI growth. A 10% probability is assigned to a bearish outcome, contingent on significant unforeseen technological disruptions or severe global economic contraction.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["Further advancements in AI models requiring even more compute power.", "Increased enterprise adoption of AI solutions across diverse industries.", "New government initiatives or funding for AI research and infrastructure.", "Strategic acquisitions or partnerships that consolidate market leadership.", "Continued strong earnings reports from key AI infrastructure providers."],
      keyRisks: ["Global economic recession impacting corporate IT budgets.", "Intensified regulatory scrutiny or anti-trust actions in the tech sector.", "Major security breaches or ethical concerns related to AI deployment.", "Supply chain disruptions for critical AI components.", "Rapid technological shifts making current hardware less competitive."],
