    outlook: "The arrest of an FBI agent for crypto theft is likely to have a lasting impact on how government agencies perceive and manage digital assets. We can anticipate increased pressure for stricter internal controls, more advanced monitoring systems, and potentially new protocols for handling cryptocurrencies involved in investigations or seizures. This event will feed into global regulatory discussions, including those in India, influencing policy decisions related to digital asset security and oversight. While not expected to cause immediate market upheaval, it reinforces the narrative that security, transparency, and accountability are paramount for the long-term health and legitimacy of the digital asset ecosystem, pushing both public and private entities towards more secure and auditable practices.",
